## Context

Twice-seen failure class: a /gaze fork goes silent between posting its
review comment and posting the verdict comment, with no error surfaced
to the caller. First seen 2026-07-11 (600s-watchdog stalls, memory
feedback_agent_stall_watchdog_recovery); recurred 2026-07-13 in raid
291-245 on PR #551 — the review comment posted at 16:24Z, the simplify
sub-agents reported, then ~30 min of quiet: no simplify commit, no
verdict, review worktree mtime frozen. Recovery that worked both times:
do NOT re-run the panel; drive /verify-gate directly on the PR, fix,
re-gate round 2. The recovery is proven; the detection and the
instruction to callers are still tribal knowledge in memory entries.
Codify both in the skill.

## Relevant files

- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` — the contract to extend (Fork execution
  contract + Branch on verdict sections; telemetry prose near
  `## Telemetry`)
- `skills/gaze/telemetry.yml` — existing threshold knobs
  (wall_seconds.warn: 900); the liveness window belongs here as a knob
- `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` — the fallback path the contract names
- memory `feedback_agent_stall_watchdog_recovery` — liveness signals
  (branch tip, worktree mtime, verdict comment); supersede its tactical
  content once codified

## Actions

1. Add a "Fork liveness" clause to `skills/gaze/SKILL.md`: after the
   review comment posts, the caller must see either the verdict comment
   or a bump log line within a bounded window (knob in telemetry.yml,
   default ~20 min; env override like the existing thresholds).
2. Name the fallback explicitly: window expired → do not re-run phases
   2-5; verify completion markers (verdict comment, branch tip motion,
   review-worktree mtime), then invoke /verify-gate directly on the PR
   and continue the normal round flow; log a bump line on the ticket.
3. Add the `liveness` knob to telemetry.yml with env override, same
   pattern as wall_seconds.
4. Extend the fork-contract adherence surface: the grep test that pins
   fork-contract wording (tests/test_verify_fork_contracts.py style)
   gains assertions that SKILL.md documents the window and the
   verify-gate fallback.

## Test

- Red first: new assertions in the fork-contract adherence test fail on
  the pre-fix SKILL.md (no liveness clause, no fallback wording).

## Invariants

- No behavior change to gaze's phases; this is caller-facing contract
  text + one knob
- The fallback never relaxes the gate: verify-gate still runs with full
  rigor, rounds still capped at 2

## Exit criteria

- [ ] SKILL.md documents the liveness window and the direct verify-gate
      fallback
- [ ] telemetry.yml carries the knob with env override
- [ ] Adherence test pins both (RED on pre-fix state)
- [ ] make check passes
